// capsules/sfn/test/src/skip.sfn — Voluntary test skips (SFN-815).
//
// Before this existed, a test that wanted to gate itself on a missing
// tool, an offline network, or an unsupported platform had exactly one
// idiom available:
//
//     if !tool_present("jq") { assert true; return; }   // "skip"
//
// That body runs, asserts successfully, and is recorded `pass`. The
// harness never learns a skip happened, so a dormant test is
// indistinguishable from a passing one — the mechanism that let SFN-807
// (system CA trust store never loads) survive a full release cycle behind
// a connectivity probe that always returned empty.
//
// `skip(reason)` is the replacement: the test is recorded `skip` with the
// reason attached, counted in the `skipped` total, and reported distinctly
// from the runner-synthesized involuntary skips (setup failed, unreachable
// after a failure, crashed before running).
//
// It does not return. The synthesized harness reports an unconditional
// `pass` the moment a test body returns normally, so a skip must leave the
// body by unwinding — `sfn_test_declare_skip` arms a pending-skip slot and
// throws, and the harness's catch path turns that into the `skip` record
// (`runtime/sfn/assert.sfn`). Statements after a `skip(...)` call are
// therefore unreachable; write it as an early exit:
//
//     test "download: follows a cross-host redirect" ![io, net] {
//         if !network_available() { skip("no outbound network"); }
//         ...
//     }
//
// A declared skip never increments the failure counter, so it cannot
// change the process exit code.
// No `![io]` on the extern itself (E0804): effects are enforced on the
// wrapping adapter below, which declares them for both.
extern fn sfn_test_declare_skip(reason_data: *u8, reason_len: i64) -> void;

// Record the running test as skipped, with `reason` explaining why it did
// not run, and abandon the rest of the test body. Honored from a test body
// and from `before_each` (where it gates that test); from the remaining
// lifecycle hooks there is no single test to attribute the skip to, so it
// is reported as a hook failure instead.
fn skip(reason: string) -> void ![io] {
    sfn_test_declare_skip(reason as *u8, reason.length);
}
